A||||7||Derek85gT||T-Tops...take off, put on?||||1||
Z||000000||Derek85gT||11-26-2001||12:35 PM||||I have a stock sunroof.  If I get a t-tops section will it work on my car?  Take off the old put on the new.  What complications or problems may I find in doing this conversion.||||reg||1
Z||000001||KissMySSFiero||11-26-2001||02:09 PM||||First you have to find the ttops.  then hope the seals arent shot.  good seals could cost as much as a halfway decent car.  i havent done the swap,  but Im pretty confident i could.   i wouldnt recomend doing it unless your a decent mechanic.  the cost of having someone do it would be worth looking for a ttop car.  My guess would be from $600 to $800 in labor.  I found a set of ttops in a junk yard but never put them in my car because i dont want to risk ruining the interior because the seals leak.  <BR>just my $.02<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <BR>88FORMULA<BR>       <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>        <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ali_Gulf_Fiero||11-26-2001||03:37 PM||||I've asked Ed Parks this same question during my visit to his factory. It's not just a question of being a decent mechanic. It's a question of having/making a large spreader to spread the forward door frame section from the aft section, plus a lot of welding. Have someone do it that has done it before. The t-top frame doesn't just place right on daintily - there's a bit of pain involved. But if you have the section, I say give Ed a call or email. Good luck!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>my cat's sitting in my scrambled eggs.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroparts.com||11-26-2001||04:28 PM||||Does Ed Parks weld the t-top frames in?<P>Man I hope not for the owner's sake!<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ali_Gulf_Fiero:<BR><B>I've asked Ed Parks this same question during my visit to his factory. It's not just a question of being a decent mechanic. It's a question of having/making a large spreader to spread the forward door frame section from the aft section, plus a lot of welding. Have someone do it that has done it before. The t-top frame doesn't just place right on daintily - there's a bit of pain involved. But if you have the section, I say give Ed a call or email. Good luck!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowfierogt||11-26-2001||07:02 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>First you have to find the ttops.  then hope the seals arent shot.  good seals could cost as much as a halfway decent car.  i havent done the swap,  but Im pretty confident i could.   i wouldnt recomend doing it unless your a decent mechanic.  the cost of having someone do it would be worth looking for a ttop car.  My guess would be from $600 to $800 in labor.  I found a set of ttops in a junk yard but never put them in my car because i dont want to risk ruining the interior because the seals leak.  <BR>just my $.02<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>want to sell your t-tops?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com/lowfierogtsig.gif">          <A HREF="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com" TARGET=_blank>http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com</A> <BR>86 1/2 GT<BR>85 GT Project<BR>87 coupe daily driver over 300k miles<p>[This message has been edited by lowfierogt (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||T-top Fiero||11-26-2001||07:25 PM||||I've done two T-top installations without needing a spreader. There is also no welding required, just plenty of 1/4" rivets.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ali_Gulf_Fiero:<BR><B>I've asked Ed Parks this same question during my visit to his factory. It's not just a question of being a decent mechanic. It's a question of having/making a large spreader to spread the forward door frame section from the aft section, plus a lot of welding. Have someone do it that has done it before. The t-top frame doesn't just place right on daintily - there's a bit of pain involved. But if you have the section, I say give Ed a call or email. Good luck!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||fieroparts.com||11-26-2001||08:46 PM||||You are 110% correct!<P><BR>48 1/4 rivets for a roof going into a car<BR>with the 3rd. brk. light and 49 w/out.<BR>On the 12 or so cars plus one more this week<BR>(my new project car that is getting a NEW KIT<BR>I might add)<BR>I have never did are welding, That's a MAJOR<BR>NO NO.<P><BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by T-top Fiero:<BR><B>I've done two T-top installations without needing a spreader. There is also no welding required, just plenty of 1/4" rivets.<P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by fieroparts.com (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||skitime||11-26-2001||08:59 PM||||Pics not many people get to see.  These might help you understand what is involved.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7090004-1.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7090005-1.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7090006-1_1.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
